==Macedonian==

===Etymology===
From Serbian Cyrillic letter [[џ#Serbian|џ]] (''dž''), adopted in 1945 by the Central Committee of [[w:League of Communists of Yugoslavia|the Communist Party of Yugoslavia]].

===Letter===
{{head|mk|letter|lower case||upper case|Џ}}

# The thirtieth letter of the Macedonian [[Cyrillic]] alphabet. Its name is {{m|mk|џ|tr=dž}} and it has a similar sound to the English '''dg''' in ''do'''dg'''e''. It is preceded by [[ч|Ч]] and followed by [[ш|Ш]].

===See also===
* {{list:Cyrillic script letters/mk}}

